WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:14.973
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

00:54.763 --> 00:55.597
Lee Min-yeong.

00:56.181 --> 00:57.015
Here.

00:58.099 --> 00:59.350
Jang Han-seul.

01:00.727 --> 01:01.644
Jang Han-seul?

01:02.562 --> 01:03.605
Jang Han-seul.

01:07.609 --> 01:08.526
Heo Do-jun.

01:08.610 --> 01:09.486
Here.

01:13.740 --> 01:17.118
I reviewed your last assignments
and left them over there.

01:17.202 --> 01:19.370
Make sure to collect them after class.

01:19.454 --> 01:20.497
Yes, Professor.

01:21.623 --> 01:22.749
Did you take notes?

01:24.417 --> 01:27.462
-Can you lend them to me next time?
-I'll send them to you.

01:32.592 --> 01:34.719
Professor!

01:37.639 --> 01:39.140
This…

01:40.391 --> 01:43.853
I mean, "trash"?
How could you write something like this?

01:43.937 --> 01:45.855
You should know, sir,

01:46.356 --> 01:48.358
that I'm an influencer.

01:49.317 --> 01:51.694
Do you even know what that means?

01:52.737 --> 01:55.782
My blog alone has over 30,000 subscribers.

01:56.491 --> 01:58.284
Do you know how many likes I get a day?

01:58.785 --> 01:59.661
Is that right?

02:00.537 --> 02:02.080
How impressive.

02:02.622 --> 02:04.415
Then that blog must be a trash can.

02:04.499 --> 02:05.458
On second thought,

02:05.542 --> 02:08.670
if it's full of writing like this,
a "landfill" might be more fitting.

02:12.632 --> 02:14.175
Twelve paragraphs

02:14.759 --> 02:17.011
and 167 sentences.

02:17.512 --> 02:20.682
You may consider this writing
since you filled the pages with whatever,

02:21.182 --> 02:24.519
but unfortunately, these pages
don't hold a single true sentence.

02:25.270 --> 02:28.523
Not a single sentence
that comes from the heart and rings true.

02:29.482 --> 02:32.402
It's just a plethora of clichés,
cheap sentimentality,

02:32.485 --> 02:35.905
and sentences copied and pasted
from other people's work.

02:36.781 --> 02:38.616
How else should I describe these words

02:38.700 --> 02:41.744
you've simply regurgitated
without grasping their meaning?

02:42.495 --> 02:45.582
If you can think of a more fitting term
than "trash," let me know.

02:48.293 --> 02:51.004
Then, going forward,
I'll try to use that word.

02:57.719 --> 02:58.928
Are we done here?

03:04.309 --> 03:05.226
What an asshole.

03:05.727 --> 03:09.272
I could just strangle him.
That soul-crushing bastard.

03:09.355 --> 03:11.232
If only his class was optional.

03:12.901 --> 03:15.361
I heard he acts like that
because he's insecure.

03:17.488 --> 03:19.657
Our seniors told me over drinks one time.

03:20.325 --> 03:22.327
Heo Mun-oh has only written one novel.

03:22.827 --> 03:24.495
Over 20 years ago, at that.

03:24.996 --> 03:28.041
But he hasn't been able to write
a second novel since.

03:28.541 --> 03:31.377
He wants to, but he can't,
no matter how hard he fucking tries.

03:31.461 --> 03:35.590
So he takes his inferiority complex
and stress out on his students.

03:36.299 --> 03:37.383
Total loser.

03:37.967 --> 03:39.510
RESEARCH IN PROGRESS
DO NOT DISTURB

03:40.845 --> 03:41.763
Mun-oh, you're here.

03:43.389 --> 03:44.933
The door was unlocked, so…

03:48.311 --> 03:51.064
Professor Park,
didn't we see each other yesterday?

03:51.147 --> 03:54.525
Well, that was yesterday, Mun-oh.
I came because I wanted to see you today.

03:54.609 --> 03:57.654
Calling me Mun-oh again.
I told you to stop using my name.

03:57.737 --> 03:59.030
Yes, Professor Heo.

04:00.114 --> 04:02.784
But I like calling you by name.

04:03.701 --> 04:05.411
Did you get home safe yesterday?

04:05.495 --> 04:08.414
-Want some coffee?
-No, I just had some.

04:09.123 --> 04:11.334
Goodness, what is this?

04:11.417 --> 04:12.919
You're so stubborn, Mun-oh.

04:13.002 --> 04:15.838
Do you still take attendance by hand?

04:16.839 --> 04:19.592
Shall I install the software for you?
It's so much easier.

04:19.676 --> 04:21.261
No, thank you.

04:21.344 --> 04:23.179
I like doing things my way.

04:24.013 --> 04:25.098
What brings you here?

04:25.598 --> 04:28.309
You must've come all the way
from Engineering for a reason.

04:28.393 --> 04:32.522
Well, I wanted to speak to you
about this yesterday, but I forgot.

04:33.022 --> 04:34.148
Mun-oh,

04:34.732 --> 04:38.319
I heard you know the author Kim Su-hun.

04:41.614 --> 04:42.448
Who?

04:43.032 --> 04:43.866
Kim Su-hun?

04:43.950 --> 04:46.411
Yes. I heard you were classmates
back in university.

04:47.203 --> 04:50.623
I had no idea
you had such impressive connections.

04:50.707 --> 04:52.250
Had I known that from the start,

04:52.333 --> 04:54.836
I would have asked you
to introduce us earlier.

04:54.919 --> 04:56.004
What do you mean?

04:56.504 --> 04:59.716
I believe I told you
about this previously.

05:00.216 --> 05:04.512
I organize the School of Engineering's
monthly cultural events.

05:04.595 --> 05:07.557
Our students are emotionally stunted,
so I thought--

05:07.640 --> 05:08.850
Just get to the point.

05:08.933 --> 05:10.727
Right, yes. The point.

05:11.477 --> 05:15.231
The point is, we're in talks
to invite Kim Su-hun next month.

05:15.315 --> 05:19.694
To give a lecture on his new novel
and have a discussion afterward.

05:19.777 --> 05:23.072
I was hoping
you could host that discussion.

05:26.659 --> 05:27.493
Well?

05:30.747 --> 05:32.874
-You want me to host the discussion?
-Yes.

05:32.957 --> 05:35.543
Mr. Kim was the one
who suggested you first.

05:40.423 --> 05:42.258
Kim Su-hun suggested me?

05:42.342 --> 05:43.634
Yes.

05:44.218 --> 05:45.428
What did he say?

05:45.511 --> 05:49.098
Just that he would feel more at ease,
and it'd be fun to chat with a friend.

05:49.807 --> 05:51.434
He said he'd come if you did it.

05:57.607 --> 05:59.108
Kim Su-hun said that?

06:00.276 --> 06:01.110
Yes.

06:07.617 --> 06:10.328
-Road's slippery. Careful.
-Can we expect a great article?

06:10.411 --> 06:14.457
Don't worry, sir. Just be ready
to print more copies of the book.

06:14.540 --> 06:15.458
Su-hun.

06:19.504 --> 06:21.839
Mun-oh! Hey, just a second.

06:22.340 --> 06:23.299
Mr. Gu?

06:23.883 --> 06:26.511
Please go ahead. I'll be right there.

06:27.011 --> 06:30.139
-Okay, sure.
-Hurry. The real interview starts now.

06:30.223 --> 06:31.057
Right.

06:31.557 --> 06:33.810
-Join us at the pork rind joint.
-You got it.

06:36.396 --> 06:40.066
I should have given you a call first.
Sorry about that.

06:40.566 --> 06:44.278
Weren't we supposed to have
dinner together today?

06:45.071 --> 06:46.531
That's what I thought.

06:46.614 --> 06:48.658
Yeah, I was thinking the same.

06:49.409 --> 06:50.868
And I have something to say.

06:50.952 --> 06:53.996
But Mr. Gu suddenly decided to join us.

06:54.580 --> 06:55.665
You know Mr. Gu, right?

06:55.748 --> 06:58.459
Of course.
What writer doesn't know Gu Yeong-ho?

06:58.960 --> 07:00.586
First time seeing him in person.

07:02.797 --> 07:03.631
So,

07:04.841 --> 07:06.134
what did you have to say?

07:06.634 --> 07:07.718
What is it?

07:09.762 --> 07:12.932
Is it about what I asked you a while ago?

07:13.724 --> 07:14.559
That favor?

07:16.644 --> 07:17.520
Yeah.

07:20.481 --> 07:22.024
I don't think I can endorse you.

07:23.192 --> 07:26.112
I think I've been too liberal
with writing endorsements lately.

07:28.823 --> 07:30.908
Liberal?

07:32.493 --> 07:35.371
Did you even read my manuscript?

07:35.455 --> 07:36.831
Of course I did.

07:38.166 --> 07:40.543
But let's talk about that later, okay?

07:40.626 --> 07:41.669
No, hey, Su-hun.

07:42.462 --> 07:43.921
Tell me now.

07:44.422 --> 07:46.507
What did you think? Just tell me.

08:49.737 --> 08:53.741
I couldn't really tell
what the author was trying to say.

08:54.909 --> 08:56.619
It made me think,

08:57.119 --> 08:59.622
why bother writing
when you have nothing to say?

09:01.707 --> 09:03.709
It's okay to live as is.

09:05.211 --> 09:07.463
But, above all else,

09:08.506 --> 09:10.550
you should relearn sentence structures.

09:25.439 --> 09:27.733
That's why
writing the first sentence is crucial.

09:31.779 --> 09:33.656
The moment the first sentence is written,

09:34.240 --> 09:38.286
the author finally takes
their first step into their story.

09:41.956 --> 09:43.374
Listen to this sentence.

09:45.585 --> 09:50.423
"How happy I am that I am gone!"

09:52.758 --> 09:53.759
"My dear friend,

09:55.344 --> 09:57.888
what a thing is the heart of man!"

09:59.056 --> 10:01.267
Anyone know
which novel's first sentence this is?

10:05.521 --> 10:06.355
No one?

10:12.069 --> 10:15.531
This is the quintessential classic.
Goethe's--

10:19.577 --> 10:20.453
Who was that?

10:22.663 --> 10:23.873
What was that noise?

10:27.084 --> 10:28.252
Apologies.

10:35.259 --> 10:39.096
That was the first sentence of Goethe's
The Sorrows of Young Werther.

10:40.014 --> 10:41.140
As you all will know,

10:41.724 --> 10:45.853
it's written in the form of letters
sent by Werther to his friend Albert…

10:45.936 --> 10:47.605
Are my classes a joke to you?

10:51.901 --> 10:53.235
Am I a joke to you?

10:56.656 --> 10:57.490
Get up.

10:58.532 --> 10:59.784
Get up.

11:01.702 --> 11:02.620
You won't?

11:04.080 --> 11:05.206
Get out!

11:07.833 --> 11:08.918
Out of my class.

11:09.001 --> 11:12.088
It's not Albert, it's Wilhelm.

11:16.133 --> 11:17.051
What?

11:18.302 --> 11:20.680
Werther's friend is Wilhelm.

11:21.681 --> 11:26.227
Albert is the fiancé of Lotte,
the woman Werther loves.

11:30.815 --> 11:32.817
The object of Werther's jealousy,

11:33.651 --> 11:36.487
admiration, and inferiority complex.

11:37.988 --> 11:38.948
But,

11:40.700 --> 11:43.619
in the sense that all of those things
are part of friendship,

11:44.912 --> 11:47.164
I guess you could say they were friends.

11:48.749 --> 11:50.459
The object of his envy,

11:52.002 --> 11:53.295
and yet, his friend.

11:59.385 --> 12:02.263
Time's up, Professor.

12:07.935 --> 12:09.103
Class dismissed.

12:15.276 --> 12:16.360
Hey, get up.

12:33.043 --> 12:35.296
FUNDAMENTALS OF WRITING
CONCEPTS AND PRACTICES

12:35.379 --> 12:36.338
PROFESSOR HEO MUN-OH

12:36.422 --> 12:37.923
ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING
LEE KANG

12:38.007 --> 12:39.341
Hey, thank you.

12:39.842 --> 12:42.052
You saved me. I almost got cooked.

12:42.845 --> 12:44.930
I'll treat you to a nice meal today.

12:45.431 --> 12:46.307
What do you want?

12:46.807 --> 12:49.185
Whatever you want. Fried chicken, pizza…

12:49.852 --> 12:53.314
But, if jealousy preceded any affection,

12:53.814 --> 12:56.901
could that relationship
still be called a friendship?

13:00.529 --> 13:03.991
I first met Se-yun in the winter
before we started school.

13:04.074 --> 13:04.909
A mere

13:05.493 --> 13:06.494
coincidence.

13:14.502 --> 13:16.420
Hurry up and clear the table.

13:17.922 --> 13:19.340
Wait, this…

13:32.436 --> 13:33.854
I held onto this for you.

13:34.355 --> 13:36.148
Thank you.

13:37.775 --> 13:39.193
I found it.

13:57.628 --> 13:58.838
Thank you so much.

13:59.588 --> 14:00.714
Thank you.

14:03.551 --> 14:06.262
Our meeting was a coincidence,
but us becoming friends

14:06.971 --> 14:08.222
wasn't a coincidence.

14:09.014 --> 14:10.182
I planned it.

14:10.266 --> 14:11.392
CODING CLUB

14:19.400 --> 14:20.484
Are you in YDOC too?

14:20.985 --> 14:22.653
They gave these as freshmen goodies.

14:25.781 --> 14:28.742
I'm Kim Se-yun, class of '25.
Library and Information Science. You?

14:29.243 --> 14:31.495
Lee Kang, class of '25.
Electronics Engineering.

14:33.080 --> 14:34.790
An engineer taking this class?

14:34.874 --> 14:36.625
Then again, it is a required course.

14:40.754 --> 14:42.506
So do you know how to code?

14:43.007 --> 14:45.926
Honestly, I'm clueless.
I joined because I like video games.

14:50.014 --> 14:51.557
Coding isn't that hard.

14:52.349 --> 14:53.350
It's easy.

14:54.059 --> 14:54.894
Really?

14:58.355 --> 15:00.316
Wow, how do you do this?

15:01.150 --> 15:02.067
Teach me.

15:02.776 --> 15:05.362
Not now. I have to go to my part-time job.

15:07.448 --> 15:09.533
How about tomorrow?
Want to come to my place?

15:10.492 --> 15:12.202
My plan worked.

15:12.703 --> 15:13.913
-Your place?
-Yeah.

15:13.996 --> 15:16.165
I finally became friends with Se-yun.

15:16.665 --> 15:19.084
Friendly enough to invite each other over.

15:19.168 --> 15:20.878
TO BE CONTINUED..

16:10.302 --> 16:14.848
Is it possible to feel nostalgia
for a place you've never been to?

16:17.601 --> 16:19.979
Is it possible to be filled with longing

16:20.729 --> 16:22.731
for someone you've never met?

16:31.240 --> 16:33.784
It was my first time at his house,
but it felt familiar.

16:34.702 --> 16:36.996
It looked just like it did in the photo.

16:39.498 --> 16:40.958
Come this way.

16:45.879 --> 16:46.797
Mom.

16:49.550 --> 16:51.093
Oh, you're home.

16:51.593 --> 16:54.096
This is my friend from my university club.

16:55.139 --> 16:56.598
I mentioned him, didn't I?

16:58.350 --> 17:00.019
Right, it's you.

17:01.061 --> 17:02.396
Nice to meet you.

17:02.938 --> 17:03.814
I'm Lee Kang.

17:05.733 --> 17:07.317
No, different from the photo.

17:07.901 --> 17:10.112
They were far more beautiful
than I'd expected.

17:10.612 --> 17:11.447
The house.

17:11.530 --> 17:12.614
-So good.
-Right?

17:12.698 --> 17:13.532
And the person.

17:14.533 --> 17:16.160
I think I'm gifted.

17:16.243 --> 17:17.494
Good job.

17:18.245 --> 17:19.288
As you should.

17:54.698 --> 17:56.075
"To be continued.."

17:56.575 --> 17:59.661
Oh my. What is this? Who wrote this?

17:59.745 --> 18:00.746
Some kid.

18:01.914 --> 18:02.998
What do you think?

18:04.249 --> 18:05.542
I'm not sure.

18:07.086 --> 18:09.963
So he purposefully approached
and befriended this boy?

18:11.340 --> 18:12.424
No, that's not it.

18:12.925 --> 18:16.345
He pretended to be his friend
so he could go to his house?

18:16.428 --> 18:20.933
My goodness. What does this kid want?
Why would he write something like this?

18:21.016 --> 18:22.559
For God's sake.

18:22.643 --> 18:23.811
What the heck?

18:23.894 --> 18:27.648
I asked for your thoughts as an expert,
yet you're saying the same thing I did.

18:28.273 --> 18:30.442
What's he thinking? You're the therapist.

18:31.485 --> 18:34.321
Well, it's too early
to make any judgments based on this.

18:36.990 --> 18:39.535
His mental state doesn't seem so complex.

18:40.786 --> 18:41.662
He's envious.

18:42.621 --> 18:45.958
He must have seen something
he desperately wanted in that other kid.

18:46.041 --> 18:50.546
And since he can't do anything about it,
he's venting through writing. Imagination.

18:53.674 --> 18:55.551
While it's a bit peculiar,

18:55.634 --> 18:58.428
being able to express these feelings
is a good thing.

19:01.682 --> 19:03.475
I'm curious what he'll write next.

19:04.059 --> 19:05.477
He's a decent writer too.

19:07.104 --> 19:08.105
Isn't it a first

19:08.605 --> 19:10.232
for you to have such a student?

19:13.360 --> 19:14.444
Yes, it is.

19:15.737 --> 19:17.739
Are you going to take him under your wing?

19:18.240 --> 19:19.658
Don't be ridiculous.

19:20.159 --> 19:20.993
I'm going.

19:21.743 --> 19:22.995
Do you know…

19:26.790 --> 19:29.042
how long it's been
since you came into my room?

19:29.543 --> 19:30.377
Do you remember?

19:34.006 --> 19:35.007
Good night.

20:00.157 --> 20:02.367
I'm curious what he'll write next.

20:03.493 --> 20:06.038
Isn't it a first for you
to have such a student?

20:07.497 --> 20:09.541
Are you going to take him under your wing?

20:34.775 --> 20:36.652
Why did you ask me to stay behind?

20:37.861 --> 20:39.238
Did you have something

20:40.614 --> 20:41.531
to say?

20:44.076 --> 20:46.620
You humiliated me
in front of the class last time.

20:47.537 --> 20:48.664
Did it feel good?

21:05.722 --> 21:07.391
Is that Kim Se-yun?

21:09.810 --> 21:10.644
Yes.

21:11.728 --> 21:14.231
Does he know
what your assignment is about?

21:14.731 --> 21:15.899
Have you shown it to him?

21:17.192 --> 21:18.026
No.

21:18.902 --> 21:21.280
I thought only you
read the assignments, Professor.

21:22.114 --> 21:23.615
You said that in the first class.

21:28.662 --> 21:29.538
Sit.

21:48.348 --> 21:49.266
What is it…

21:51.393 --> 21:53.020
that you want to write about?

21:53.812 --> 21:55.188
What are you trying to write?

21:56.148 --> 21:57.190
What do you mean?

21:57.691 --> 22:00.569
It's an assignment,
so I just wrote whatever I felt like.

22:01.153 --> 22:01.987
As you told us to.

22:02.988 --> 22:04.323
No.

22:06.575 --> 22:09.411
You know what I'm asking you.

22:10.829 --> 22:12.164
Let's not play dumb.

22:22.841 --> 22:23.967
You…

22:26.928 --> 22:28.430
envy Kim Se-yun, don't you?

22:30.057 --> 22:31.683
And you want to be him?

22:33.352 --> 22:35.562
That's why you wrote this, isn't it?

22:40.734 --> 22:41.943
But you know,

22:43.528 --> 22:45.280
in Kim Se-yun's assignment,

22:45.822 --> 22:47.741
there's not a single word about you.

22:48.617 --> 22:50.702
He doesn't seem to care at all

22:50.786 --> 22:52.996
whether you envy him or not.

22:53.955 --> 22:55.624
You're the only one who's suffering.

23:00.212 --> 23:01.671
Do you know it too?

23:03.715 --> 23:04.800
That feeling?

23:15.394 --> 23:19.106
So are you suggesting
that I should write about something else?

23:21.066 --> 23:25.070
-There's nothing else I want to write.
-No, write. Write about this.

23:25.153 --> 23:28.323
My point is that you should keep writing.

23:28.407 --> 23:30.158
Even if it's hard, just write.

23:31.576 --> 23:33.620
What's important is wanting to write.

23:37.749 --> 23:38.834
You have talent.

23:43.630 --> 23:44.506
And

23:45.632 --> 23:48.468
take one-on-one literature lessons
from me. Once a week.

23:49.261 --> 23:50.554
-One-on-one?
-Yes.

23:50.637 --> 23:51.763
One-on-one.

23:54.182 --> 23:56.309
I'm saying I'll make time for you.

23:56.393 --> 23:57.686
What? Don't you get it?

23:57.769 --> 23:59.104
No, I don't think I can.

24:00.856 --> 24:02.482
I have several part-time jobs.

24:05.193 --> 24:06.903
And money matters more to me.

24:16.413 --> 24:17.289
Then,

24:18.707 --> 24:22.169
what if I pay you as much as you earn
from one of your part-time jobs?

24:30.135 --> 24:30.969
Why?

24:34.181 --> 24:35.056
Do you like me?

24:39.186 --> 24:41.563
Crazy bastard. You're talking nonsense.

24:50.197 --> 24:51.031
Lee Kang.

24:54.159 --> 24:57.704
Quit talking nonsense, you punk,
and listen to me carefully.

24:59.873 --> 25:02.167
You can't be Kim Se-yun,

25:02.709 --> 25:06.379
but you can write as much as you want
about your desire to become him.

25:07.839 --> 25:10.050
As long as you can sublimate that feeling.

25:10.717 --> 25:13.428
That's what literature is.
That's the power of literature.

25:16.515 --> 25:18.058
I want to help you

25:18.141 --> 25:21.895
so that the things you write
don't end up as mere scribbles

25:22.812 --> 25:24.523
but become a coherent story.

25:26.733 --> 25:27.567
Because

25:28.068 --> 25:30.195
talent is a rare thing,

25:30.862 --> 25:32.489
and I'm your teacher.

25:34.449 --> 25:37.911
All right, Professor.
I'll quit one of my part-time jobs.

25:44.251 --> 25:51.049
ALL RIGHT, TEACHER
I'LL QUIT ONE OF MY PART-TIME JOBS

26:32.090 --> 26:33.091
Why are you grinning?

26:34.342 --> 26:35.927
I just find it funny.

26:36.761 --> 26:40.056
Literature lessons?
I didn't think you'd actually do it.

26:41.766 --> 26:44.561
Anyway, it's nice to see you
in good spirits.

26:44.644 --> 26:47.522
Didn't you say you were running late
for your appointment?

26:48.023 --> 26:49.107
You should get going.

26:51.151 --> 26:53.778
Still, I don't quite like you
doing the lessons here.

26:53.862 --> 26:57.115
Why at home?
You could do them on campus or at a café.

26:58.283 --> 27:02.537
I told you, if we do them outside,
people will see us and start talking.

27:04.331 --> 27:08.209
And when you meet Professor Park
and Seong-hui, you can't tell them, okay?

27:08.710 --> 27:09.544
Say I was busy.

27:09.628 --> 27:13.173
Oh, all right. Why do you always
insist on being so secretive?

27:15.508 --> 27:17.302
I'm off. Enjoy your lesson.

27:17.385 --> 27:18.428
Sure.

28:17.404 --> 28:18.238
Hey.

28:19.906 --> 28:20.740
Come on in.

28:33.586 --> 28:34.462
This way.

28:42.429 --> 28:43.930
Why aren't you coming in?

28:55.692 --> 28:58.278
Why do you look so down?
You're here to study.

28:58.820 --> 29:00.780
You haven't even greeted me properly.

29:02.782 --> 29:03.992
I did say hi.

29:04.909 --> 29:06.661
You little… Sit.

29:09.080 --> 29:09.914
Actually…

29:13.084 --> 29:16.504
something's been weighing on me,
and I thought I'd tell you over the phone,

29:17.005 --> 29:19.716
but I figured I should tell you in person.

29:21.676 --> 29:22.761
What do you mean?

29:25.221 --> 29:26.848
I can't take these lessons.

29:29.350 --> 29:30.185
The thing is,

29:31.019 --> 29:33.646
something happened
when I was at Se-yun's place yesterday.

29:33.730 --> 29:37.317
I might not be able to go there again,
which means I won't be able to write.

29:37.859 --> 29:39.861
Then these classes would be pointless, so…

29:41.905 --> 29:42.739
Wait.

29:43.740 --> 29:46.618
Take your time and explain.
Why, what happened?

29:52.832 --> 29:55.210
Do you remember
I wrote about the coding club?

29:55.919 --> 29:56.753
Yeah.

29:57.462 --> 30:00.006
Our club has a competition
coming up in two weeks.

30:00.507 --> 30:02.926
The preliminaries
of a national tournament for clubs.

30:06.429 --> 30:08.973
Se-yun and I were going to enter
as a team,

30:09.474 --> 30:12.685
so I went over to his place yesterday
to study together, but…

30:13.269 --> 30:14.103
But?

30:14.938 --> 30:16.314
Try up to this page.

30:16.397 --> 30:17.232
Okay.

30:18.358 --> 30:20.985
-I'm going to the bathroom.
-Sure, go ahead.

30:57.438 --> 30:59.399
I was only going to the bathroom,

30:59.899 --> 31:01.693
but I suddenly got curious.

31:21.170 --> 31:24.132
Frankly, it was wrong of me.

32:54.138 --> 32:55.264
I'm sorry.

32:56.599 --> 32:58.309
I couldn't find the bathroom.

33:00.269 --> 33:03.690
I see. I thought you were my Yun.

33:03.773 --> 33:05.566
There's also a bathroom upstairs.

33:05.650 --> 33:07.819
And one for guests by the front door.

33:09.362 --> 33:11.197
Yes, understood.

33:12.031 --> 33:13.574
I'll use one of those from now on.

33:19.122 --> 33:22.417
Even though I was out of line,
Se-yun's mom was kind.

33:22.917 --> 33:25.712
She didn't get mad,
was considerate and gracious,

33:26.212 --> 33:28.172
and didn't seem upset
during dinner, either.

33:28.673 --> 33:30.508
-It's hot.
-Okay.

33:33.928 --> 33:35.680
What's taking you so long? Come on.

33:36.180 --> 33:38.099
The kids are hungry and waiting.

33:38.599 --> 33:40.184
Yes, be right there.

33:47.984 --> 33:52.822
So you're Se-yun's new friend.
Nice to meet you. Lee Kang, right?

33:54.073 --> 33:54.907
Hello.

33:54.991 --> 33:55.867
Have a seat.

33:59.871 --> 34:01.789
I hear you're great with computers.

34:02.623 --> 34:05.126
You're all Se-yun talks about these days.

34:06.210 --> 34:07.462
It's true.

34:08.421 --> 34:10.590
He's had so many friends
but never like this.

34:10.673 --> 34:12.592
I don't talk about him that much.

34:12.675 --> 34:16.888
The truth is, I'm only able to enter
this competition thanks to Kang.

34:17.388 --> 34:19.974
Even all the seniors
are floored by his skills.

34:21.017 --> 34:22.977
Hey, why are you exaggerating?

34:23.061 --> 34:23.936
Exaggerating?

34:24.520 --> 34:26.647
Anyway, please take good care of Se-yun.

34:27.148 --> 34:30.234
His dream is to become
a programmer now, all of a sudden.

34:31.319 --> 34:33.821
Had we known,
we'd have made him study engineering.

34:35.031 --> 34:36.240
Okay. Let's eat.

34:38.201 --> 34:39.202
Let's say grace first.

34:39.702 --> 34:42.872
In the name of the Father,
of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.

34:42.955 --> 34:45.875
Bless us, O Lord, and these gifts,
which we are about to receive

34:45.958 --> 34:47.627
from thy bounty…

34:47.710 --> 34:51.172
But, as I was about to head home,
I found out the truth.

34:51.672 --> 34:53.341
How she really felt about me.

34:53.424 --> 34:57.178
I don't know. There's something
suspicious and sneaky about him.

34:57.845 --> 35:00.306
You know how everyone gives off a vibe.

35:00.807 --> 35:04.936
I felt it from the first time I met him.
I wish he'd stop coming over.

35:06.229 --> 35:07.271
What is it now?

35:09.732 --> 35:11.609
What's got you all worked up this time?

35:13.903 --> 35:16.614
We can't exactly ban a friend
who Se-yun likes.

35:17.115 --> 35:19.117
All we can do is just watch over him.

35:20.368 --> 35:23.663
Do you know what happened earlier today?
He was in our bedroom…

35:25.706 --> 35:30.253
I'm just saying I'd prefer our Yun
to be friends with someone

35:30.795 --> 35:32.547
more cheerful and lively.

35:33.297 --> 35:34.465
Seriously?

35:35.550 --> 35:38.094
I thought the kid was fine. Seemed smart.

35:38.970 --> 35:42.932
Well then, let's at least leave them be
until after the competition.

35:43.683 --> 35:45.101
What if they win an award?

35:46.477 --> 35:50.690
They say awards at competitions like that
stand out on job applications.

35:51.190 --> 35:53.609
That's been on my mind too.

35:54.402 --> 35:55.486
All right.

35:55.987 --> 35:58.322
If it means it's going to help our son.

35:59.073 --> 36:01.492
-Let's revisit this after the competition.
-Yeah.

36:13.671 --> 36:15.840
What'd you do that for, huh?

36:15.923 --> 36:17.758
I know what I did was wrong.

36:20.094 --> 36:22.805
So, are you telling me

36:24.223 --> 36:27.560
that you have to win that competition
or whatever it's called

36:28.060 --> 36:30.271
in order to keep going over to his place?

36:30.855 --> 36:32.815
Yes. That's how it is.

36:33.399 --> 36:36.652
Then win it. Just do it.
You're good at programming, aren't you?

36:37.153 --> 36:38.863
Don't talk about what you don't know.

36:38.946 --> 36:41.449
I may be better than Se-yun,
but I don't stand a chance.

36:46.495 --> 36:47.788
Hey, but it's not like

36:48.331 --> 36:51.417
you have to go inside that house
in order to be able to write.

36:53.502 --> 36:56.297
What would I feel or write about
if I don't?

36:56.380 --> 36:57.590
That was my inspiration.

36:59.634 --> 37:00.635
You're right.

37:01.344 --> 37:02.470
Yes, that's true.

37:03.638 --> 37:04.472
That's true.

37:07.141 --> 37:08.517
Then what should we do?

37:09.101 --> 37:12.813
We need to come up with a good idea…

37:14.732 --> 37:16.984
There might be a way, but…

37:19.111 --> 37:19.946
What is it?

37:28.788 --> 37:31.749
Forget it. You couldn't do it, Mr. Heo.

37:32.250 --> 37:35.670
What are you talking about, punk?
What couldn't I do? Tell me.

37:43.886 --> 37:45.054
The competition problems.

37:46.597 --> 37:47.723
Competition problems?

37:51.185 --> 37:52.311
What about them?

38:07.368 --> 38:08.452
You don't mean…

38:11.414 --> 38:13.374
You're not asking me…

38:15.167 --> 38:16.627
to steal the competition problems…

38:18.921 --> 38:19.964
are you?

38:21.757 --> 38:24.051
I can't think of any other way
out of this.

38:29.307 --> 38:30.433
Are you crazy?

38:32.935 --> 38:34.228
You're a lunatic.

38:38.733 --> 38:39.817
You little punk.

38:41.444 --> 38:44.739
I'm your teacher
and a professor at that school!

38:45.406 --> 38:47.700
How dare you ask such a thing!

38:52.163 --> 38:53.581
Hey, get out.

38:54.623 --> 38:57.752
Get out of here! I'm not interested
in giving you lessons anymore.

38:58.336 --> 39:00.463
You're a real piece of work, aren't you?

39:02.340 --> 39:03.424
Get out!

39:07.803 --> 39:09.263
Then it can't be helped.

39:11.057 --> 39:13.017
I'll just forget about
your teaching offer.

39:22.151 --> 39:23.569
Why, that punk…

39:25.363 --> 39:27.531
What the hell is wrong with him?

39:40.419 --> 39:42.463
Why didn't you hand in your assignment?

39:43.214 --> 39:44.924
I had nothing to write about.

39:53.307 --> 39:54.183
Hey, Lee Kang!

39:55.393 --> 39:59.313
Are you really not handing something in?
At this rate, I won't help you…

40:01.899 --> 40:02.733
Hey.

40:04.402 --> 40:05.277
Hey!

40:05.361 --> 40:06.862
ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING
LEE KANG

40:23.712 --> 40:27.716
GUEST LECTURE WITH AUTHOR KIM SU-HUN

40:29.051 --> 40:30.970
AUTHOR OF EYES OF THE HOUSE

41:08.799 --> 41:09.842
Hey, Professor Park.

41:10.342 --> 41:11.927
Hey, Mun-oh! I mean…

41:12.428 --> 41:14.680
Professor Heo, where are you?

41:15.347 --> 41:16.307
Well…

41:16.390 --> 41:18.976
Mr. Kim is already here waiting for you.

41:19.477 --> 41:22.104
You should have a chat over coffee
before the lecture.

41:22.188 --> 41:23.355
Is that so?

41:23.439 --> 41:26.609
Deary me.
You see, I'm on my way right now.

41:27.109 --> 41:30.154
About ten minutes?
I think I'll be there in about ten.

41:30.237 --> 41:34.700
Tell him to have a cup of tea
and wait a little longer, yeah?

41:35.201 --> 41:37.620
Sorry about that. I'll be there soon.

41:38.579 --> 41:39.872
Okay, see you soon.

41:52.134 --> 41:53.928
Wow, long time no see.

41:54.803 --> 41:57.806
-It's been a while.
-It has indeed. Been a while.

41:57.890 --> 42:00.017
When was the last time we saw each other?

42:00.100 --> 42:02.061
Life's so busy. I can't remember…

42:02.561 --> 42:03.604
Let me see.

42:03.687 --> 42:06.857
When was it? I can't quite remember.

42:08.317 --> 42:11.028
I guess it really is nice
meeting old friends.

42:11.111 --> 42:14.323
Why, I've never seen Professor Heo
with such a big smile.

42:14.406 --> 42:15.783
Is that so?

42:17.326 --> 42:20.371
Yeah, I'm happy too. It's good to see you.

42:21.956 --> 42:23.165
You haven't changed.

42:24.041 --> 42:28.504
Over seven full-length novels
and four short story collections,

42:28.587 --> 42:30.381
you've delved deep

42:31.173 --> 42:34.635
into the complexity of the human psyche.

42:34.718 --> 42:37.596
But in your latest work,
Eyes of the House,

42:37.680 --> 42:39.640
you've taken an entirely new approach

42:40.140 --> 42:42.977
by incorporating the techniques
of mystery novels.

42:43.060 --> 42:43.894
That's right.

42:44.728 --> 42:46.897
I borrowed from the mystery genre.

42:47.523 --> 42:49.567
But while your standard mystery novel

42:50.067 --> 42:54.446
focuses on solving the case,
I was interested in something different.

42:54.947 --> 42:59.368
I broke every scene down into fragments,
including the murder scene,

42:59.451 --> 43:02.997
and scrambled them so it's difficult
to tell the sequence of events.

43:04.415 --> 43:08.252
Because what was important to me
wasn't who the culprit was,

43:08.752 --> 43:10.796
nor the resolution
and conclusion of the case.

43:10.879 --> 43:15.175
It was the multi-layered
human relationships surrounding it.

43:17.886 --> 43:19.013
You all got that, right?

43:20.431 --> 43:21.515
Well, I understood.

43:23.642 --> 43:26.520
Yes, it's truly remarkable.

43:26.604 --> 43:28.314
That's why most readers

43:29.023 --> 43:32.192
have reviewed this book
as "very novel" and "refreshing."

43:33.611 --> 43:36.280
But…

43:37.906 --> 43:38.991
But

43:40.326 --> 43:41.535
some people…

43:45.205 --> 43:46.040
Some people?

43:47.833 --> 43:52.254
Well, some people say… Put differently…

43:54.214 --> 43:58.552
This may be a little uncomfortable
for you to hear,

43:59.053 --> 44:02.598
but since this is a place
for free discussion,

44:02.681 --> 44:03.932
I'll say it.

44:06.685 --> 44:09.605
"With this novel,
Kim Su-hun is catering to the masses."

44:10.105 --> 44:14.985
Well, the fact is that there are some
who hold critical opinions like this.

44:18.280 --> 44:21.992
Of course, this isn't my personal opinion.

44:22.076 --> 44:24.662
Before I came to this lecture hall today,

44:24.745 --> 44:28.207
I received a few questions
from some students.

44:28.832 --> 44:30.793
This was one of the questions.

44:32.252 --> 44:33.504
Just a moment.

44:33.587 --> 44:35.172
So…

44:36.256 --> 44:39.385
Let's see.

44:39.468 --> 44:41.720
Where is it? Oh, here it is.

44:42.262 --> 44:43.639
So,

44:44.807 --> 44:47.017
this was the student's question.

44:48.102 --> 44:49.770
"Mr. Kim Su-hun,

44:49.853 --> 44:53.816
you've long established
a reputation in literary fiction,

44:53.899 --> 44:58.987
so I had great respect for you
and was a huge fan of yours."

44:59.655 --> 45:04.952
"But I was quite disappointed when you
suddenly came out with a mystery novel."

45:05.452 --> 45:09.248
"Is it perhaps because you don't have
any stories of your own left to tell

45:09.748 --> 45:14.128
that you had no choice
but to cater to the masses?"

45:14.878 --> 45:16.505
That's pretty harsh.

45:17.464 --> 45:19.800
"If you don't have
any stories left to tell…

45:21.802 --> 45:22.886
wouldn't it be better

45:23.679 --> 45:28.058
to stop writing altogether?"

45:28.976 --> 45:30.102
Something like that.

45:31.478 --> 45:33.230
Which student asked this question?

45:41.822 --> 45:44.116
Is this, by any chance,
your opinion, Professor Heo?

45:44.742 --> 45:46.869
What? No, it's…

45:47.536 --> 45:49.079
I'm just messing with you.

45:49.705 --> 45:52.458
I'd like to thank the fan who asked this,
whoever you are.

45:52.541 --> 45:57.004
Sounds like you're very interested in me
and have followed my work for a long time.

45:57.504 --> 45:59.089
To answer your question,

45:59.715 --> 46:02.009
yes, you're right. Catering to the masses.

46:03.761 --> 46:06.638
The verb "to cater to"
could be interpreted two ways.

46:06.722 --> 46:10.726
"To satisfy the desires or needs
of the general public."

46:11.310 --> 46:13.520
That can be interpreted negatively
as pandering,

46:13.604 --> 46:15.105
but it could be a positive.

46:15.856 --> 46:17.357
"Finding common ground."

46:17.858 --> 46:20.569
According to that second definition,

46:21.069 --> 46:22.946
it is essential to cater to all in art.

46:23.489 --> 46:26.825
What could be more exciting
than the author and the readers

46:26.909 --> 46:29.286
finding common ground?

46:31.038 --> 46:34.625
What truly matters is not "what"
but always "how."

46:35.209 --> 46:37.961
A flexible and multi-faceted
perspective is crucial.

46:38.921 --> 46:41.590
If you insist on sticking to
a world you're familiar with,

46:41.673 --> 46:43.759
your creativity will inevitably wither.

46:44.635 --> 46:48.430
That is why I will continue to tell
new stories, experiment with new forms,

46:48.514 --> 46:52.267
and strive to become even better
at catering to the masses.

47:05.197 --> 47:07.533
The atmosphere was great today, wasn't it?

47:07.616 --> 47:10.577
-The students' response was just…
-It was amazing.

47:10.661 --> 47:11.829
-Mr. Kim.
-Thanks.

47:12.329 --> 47:16.250
Of all the events we've organized so far,
today's had the highest attendance.

47:16.333 --> 47:18.710
The dean was so excited.

47:19.461 --> 47:21.797
Thanks to you,
I got a lot of compliments today.

47:21.880 --> 47:26.969
Oh, please. It's all thanks to you
and Professor Heo, who hosted.

47:27.845 --> 47:31.431
But more than anything,
the students were listening so intently,

47:31.515 --> 47:33.892
I got very excited
and talked way more than usual.

47:33.976 --> 47:36.895
-Thank you.
-The students really were great today.

47:36.979 --> 47:39.064
Why don't they act like that
in my lectures?

47:39.565 --> 47:40.983
You just have to do better.

47:41.066 --> 47:43.026
Let's have a drink. It's an honor.

47:43.110 --> 47:43.944
Yes.

47:44.027 --> 47:46.029
-Lovely to meet you.
-Truly an honor.

47:53.829 --> 47:56.790
Why have you been so quiet, Professor Heo?

47:57.749 --> 48:01.587
Not at all. I've just been listening
and enjoying your conversation.

48:01.670 --> 48:03.714
Right. You two are friends, aren't you?

48:03.797 --> 48:05.382
Yes, from university.

48:07.301 --> 48:08.552
Do you enjoy teaching?

48:10.345 --> 48:12.222
How could it possibly be fun?

48:13.307 --> 48:18.896
Mr. Kim, your daughter's pen name
is Lee I-pil, isn't it?

48:18.979 --> 48:22.232
She made her debut last year
with Seventeen Green Wings.

48:22.316 --> 48:23.692
Wow, really?

48:23.775 --> 48:26.737
That writer who made a clean sweep
of the literary debut awards

48:26.820 --> 48:29.072
was your daughter? Wow.

48:29.156 --> 48:30.824
I think I've heard about it too.

48:30.908 --> 48:33.911
I guess there are no secrets
in this world.

48:33.994 --> 48:37.080
I even came up with her pen name
so people wouldn't know.

48:37.164 --> 48:39.666
Wow, how impressive.

48:39.750 --> 48:42.127
I guess literary talent
runs in the family.

48:42.210 --> 48:44.504
You must be so proud. I'm so jealous.

48:45.380 --> 48:50.218
A talented child and your career?
You really do have it all.

49:47.275 --> 49:48.276
Mr. Heo.

49:49.820 --> 49:50.904
What are you…

49:54.950 --> 49:55.867
You work here?

49:56.618 --> 49:57.452
Yes.

49:59.037 --> 50:00.831
You must be here with someone.

50:01.832 --> 50:02.791
Yeah.

50:04.334 --> 50:06.503
What were you scribbling while working?

50:11.591 --> 50:12.467
This is just…

50:13.552 --> 50:16.430
Just what, punk?
You don't even turn in your assignments.

50:20.308 --> 50:21.685
Actually, I was thinking…

50:23.979 --> 50:25.981
of applying to a writing contest.

50:26.606 --> 50:28.275
Literary debut awards.

50:29.151 --> 50:32.320
I heard the prize money can be decent,
so I thought I'd give it a shot.

50:32.904 --> 50:34.322
What, a contest?

50:35.240 --> 50:36.825
Mr. Heo, you told me

50:38.243 --> 50:39.411
that I have talent.

50:41.830 --> 50:45.500
But I haven't found a story
that I want to write just yet.

51:03.643 --> 51:05.729
Literary debut awards.

51:10.108 --> 51:11.735
That rascal.

51:15.947 --> 51:17.991
What a load of crap.

51:25.791 --> 51:27.209
LITERARY DEBUT AWARD
LEE KANG

51:28.418 --> 51:30.837
Thank you. Thank you so much.

51:33.507 --> 51:36.760
But this award truly belongs

51:37.427 --> 51:38.720
to someone else.

51:38.804 --> 51:40.472
"You have talent."

51:40.972 --> 51:43.517
The person who opened my eyes
with those words.

51:44.351 --> 51:45.811
The person who taught me

51:46.311 --> 51:49.481
what literature is,
and beyond that, what it means to live.

51:53.443 --> 51:54.694
My mentor, Mr. Heo Mun-oh.

51:57.948 --> 51:59.491
Thank you so much.

53:00.886 --> 53:01.928
Hey.

53:03.555 --> 53:07.309
Do you think the literary debut awards
are child's play?

53:09.019 --> 53:11.646
You don't stand a chance
with your skills, you punk.

53:24.868 --> 53:25.869
Then…

53:28.663 --> 53:31.249
If you have them,

53:31.333 --> 53:34.878
the problems
for that competition or whatever…

53:38.715 --> 53:41.468
will you start taking writing seriously?

53:44.179 --> 53:46.097
And take the literature lessons again?

53:58.818 --> 53:59.653
Then, kid,

54:00.403 --> 54:03.448
what do I need to do? Tell me!

54:15.210 --> 54:16.962
Are you sure you're okay with this?

54:18.296 --> 54:21.383
It's actually pretty simple.
You just need to do as I say.

54:21.883 --> 54:23.927
Yeah, well, what do I need to do exactly?

54:24.010 --> 54:26.346
Go to Professor Park Hyeong-jong's office.

54:27.013 --> 54:28.098
Park Hyeong-jong?

54:28.848 --> 54:30.767
-Professor Park from Engineering?
-Yes.

54:30.850 --> 54:33.770
He's head of the competition's
problem selection committee.

54:34.980 --> 54:37.440
That guy just needs to have
his fingers in every pie.

54:38.024 --> 54:41.695
Wait. How did you know
that I'm acquainted with Professor Park?

54:42.279 --> 54:44.447
Do you think I'd have asked otherwise?

54:44.531 --> 54:46.449
I've seen you two talking before.

54:46.950 --> 54:48.159
-Enjoy your meal.
-Yeah.

54:48.243 --> 54:49.244
Eat up.

54:49.869 --> 54:51.746
-Here you are.
-Thank you.

54:55.375 --> 54:57.544
-Enjoy your meal.
-You too.

55:01.339 --> 55:02.299
Professor Park.

55:03.466 --> 55:05.260
Mun-oh! Come join me.

55:06.011 --> 55:07.971
-You're eating quite late.
-As are you.

55:08.054 --> 55:11.516
And after I'm in Professor Park's office?
What do I do once I'm there?

55:11.599 --> 55:12.434
This is nice.

55:12.517 --> 55:16.771
The competition is tomorrow,
so the problems will be on his computer.

55:16.855 --> 55:19.899
All you need to do is copy them
onto a USB drive. Simple, right?

55:19.983 --> 55:23.320
Punk, you call that simple?
How would I get into his computer?

55:23.820 --> 55:25.488
I'd need to know his password!

55:25.572 --> 55:29.909
Right, that's why Professor Park
needs to unlock it himself.

55:33.496 --> 55:34.331
Professor Park.

55:36.708 --> 55:40.170
I have a favor to ask.

55:40.795 --> 55:43.548
Wow, you've never asked
for a favor before.

55:44.716 --> 55:45.800
Go ahead.

55:45.884 --> 55:47.469
It's just that

55:47.552 --> 55:52.349
I was thinking it's about time
I updated the way I take attendance.

55:52.432 --> 55:53.558
-Really?
-Yes.

55:53.641 --> 55:56.061
You told me about it once before.

55:56.144 --> 55:58.521
Wow, this is music to my ears.

55:59.022 --> 56:01.441
Yeah, it's about time you updated it.

56:01.524 --> 56:04.861
Okay, I'll go to your office tomorrow
and install it for you.

56:04.944 --> 56:06.404
No, not my office.

56:07.322 --> 56:10.158
I'd like to do it at your office.

56:10.241 --> 56:15.205
Shouldn't I at least see
how it's run first?

56:16.998 --> 56:17.832
Really?

56:17.916 --> 56:21.544
I don't really have time today,
so come to my office tomorrow.

56:21.628 --> 56:23.213
-I'll show you.
-Tomorrow?

56:23.713 --> 56:26.174
No, tomorrow's too late.
It has to be done today.

56:28.134 --> 56:32.389
I have something to attend to tomorrow,
so I'll be a bit busy.

56:33.264 --> 56:35.934
Can't I just stop by for a bit today?

56:36.518 --> 56:38.853
-Today? Now?
-Yeah, it won't take long.

56:39.437 --> 56:41.773
Okay, well, I have a little time to spare.

56:41.856 --> 56:44.734
-Let's go, then.
-Okay. Let's swing by now, then.

56:44.818 --> 56:46.903
-Strike while the iron is hot.
-Now?

56:46.986 --> 56:49.197
Yeah, just for a bit.
This food is terrible.

56:49.280 --> 56:50.407
I barely ate anything.

56:50.490 --> 56:53.243
It's terrible.
I'll treat you to some duck later.

56:53.326 --> 56:54.160
But…

56:54.661 --> 56:56.079
-Let's go, okay?
-But this food…

56:56.162 --> 56:57.455
-Come on.
-TA Kim.

56:57.539 --> 56:58.915
-Yes?
-Our trays, please.

56:58.998 --> 57:00.041
-Sure.
-Sorry.

57:00.125 --> 57:01.626
-Sorry.
-Goodbye.

57:01.709 --> 57:03.878
I blathered on
for about 30 minutes, I think?

57:03.962 --> 57:07.465
But when the show aired,
I was only on for about a minute or two.

57:07.966 --> 57:12.429
And after coming all the way to my office
and begging me to do it.

57:14.013 --> 57:15.765
It's truly convenient.

57:16.266 --> 57:18.017
-Hello.
-Hi, Mi-jin.

57:18.560 --> 57:20.145
No, I can't do it.

57:20.228 --> 57:22.272
I just don't think I can do it.

57:22.355 --> 57:25.483
How could I, an educator, do such a thing?

57:25.567 --> 57:27.485
It's too late to say that now.

57:30.155 --> 57:32.115
Mun-oh, are you feeling unwell?

57:33.908 --> 57:35.952
Professor Park.

57:36.619 --> 57:39.664
I'm sorry, but I need to go
to the bathroom quickly.

57:40.206 --> 57:42.459
All right. Be back soon.

57:42.542 --> 57:43.668
-Okay.
-I'll be inside.

57:43.751 --> 57:45.003
Yeah, sorry about that.

57:59.809 --> 58:01.644
There's no need to feel guilty.

58:02.145 --> 58:04.606
I'm not going to participate
in the finals anyway,

58:04.689 --> 58:07.066
so we wouldn't be hurting anybody.

58:13.406 --> 58:16.993
Hit this,
and I'll log in with my account first.

58:17.744 --> 58:19.078
Once you're logged in…

58:19.954 --> 58:21.289
The problem is,

58:21.789 --> 58:24.250
I'm not sure how we could get him

58:24.334 --> 58:25.418
out of his office.

58:25.502 --> 58:26.544
For that,

58:27.545 --> 58:28.838
I've come up with a plan.

58:28.922 --> 58:29.756
What?

58:30.256 --> 58:31.925
You have? What is it?

58:32.008 --> 58:36.262
…the attendance scores
will automatically be added to the final…

58:37.514 --> 58:39.474
-What's wrong?
-My chest.

58:39.974 --> 58:42.894
-It's coming.
-Mun-oh, what's wrong?

58:43.520 --> 58:44.812
I feel it coming.

58:44.896 --> 58:45.730
What…

58:46.231 --> 58:47.982
Are you okay? Should I call 911?

58:48.066 --> 58:50.777
No, you don't have to call them.

58:50.860 --> 58:52.654
-But…
-Just give me a minute.

58:54.113 --> 58:55.156
What is it?

58:55.240 --> 58:57.534
My meds must be in my car.

58:58.034 --> 58:59.786
Hey, what meds?

58:59.869 --> 59:01.079
For my angina.

59:01.663 --> 59:03.540
Mun-oh, you have angina?

59:03.623 --> 59:05.291
Okay, just wait here a minute.

59:05.375 --> 59:06.292
I'm so sorry.

59:06.376 --> 59:08.086
-Just wait here.
-I'm sorry.

59:08.169 --> 59:09.128
I'll be right back!

59:09.921 --> 59:11.631
-Hello, Professor.
-Hey, yeah.

59:25.520 --> 59:27.897
-What medicine is it?
-You don't need to know, punk.

59:29.482 --> 59:30.567
It's for hemorrhoids.

59:36.197 --> 59:37.490
Oh man, come on.

59:37.574 --> 59:38.658
Damn it!

59:40.243 --> 59:44.455
But the parking lot is too close.
It won't take him more than five minutes.

59:44.539 --> 59:45.915
Five minutes is plenty.

59:46.416 --> 59:47.792
Just tell me the file name.

59:48.793 --> 59:52.005
The thing is, I don't know
what the file name would be.

59:52.088 --> 59:52.922
What?

59:53.673 --> 59:55.133
You damn punk!

01:00:13.109 --> 01:00:15.570
You're going to end up making me ill.

01:00:20.199 --> 01:00:21.618
Damn it, where is it?

01:00:24.746 --> 01:00:25.705
Let's see.

01:00:39.344 --> 01:00:40.762
Oh, here it is!

01:00:40.845 --> 01:00:42.930
YEONSEO UNIVERSITY
PROGRAMMING COMPETITION

01:00:43.014 --> 01:00:44.265
ANSWERS
COMPETITION PROBLEMS

01:00:44.766 --> 01:00:46.142
-Hello.
-Yeah.

01:00:48.394 --> 01:00:49.896
Hey, yeah.

01:01:10.833 --> 01:01:11.834
Got it.

01:01:12.585 --> 01:01:13.544
It's done.

01:01:19.133 --> 01:01:20.343
Damn it.

01:01:24.472 --> 01:01:26.349
Why is it so slow?

01:01:28.017 --> 01:01:29.143
50%.

01:01:30.436 --> 01:01:32.188
Come on, hurry.

01:01:35.817 --> 01:01:37.777
Okay. Almost there.

01:01:37.860 --> 01:01:39.612
Hurry.

01:01:44.117 --> 01:01:45.576
Just a little more.

01:01:51.958 --> 01:01:53.251
Mun-oh, your meds.

01:01:53.835 --> 01:01:54.794
Right.

01:01:54.877 --> 01:01:55.795
Are you okay?

01:01:58.089 --> 01:02:00.007
-Are you okay?
-Thanks, Professor Park.

01:02:00.091 --> 01:02:02.635
I feel much better, thanks to you.

01:02:02.719 --> 01:02:05.847
You see, it just swoops in.

01:02:05.930 --> 01:02:08.182
-Yes?
-Then it flies away.

01:02:09.308 --> 01:02:10.393
Sorry for the bother.

01:02:10.476 --> 01:02:11.310
No, it's…

01:02:11.394 --> 01:02:13.146
Oh, and Professor Park.

01:02:13.229 --> 01:02:15.982
I thought about it,

01:02:16.065 --> 01:02:18.568
and maybe my way is better after all.

01:02:19.068 --> 01:02:19.902
Sorry?

01:02:19.986 --> 01:02:21.571
-Thanks anyway.
-Yeah.

01:02:22.071 --> 01:02:23.531
-Are you sure you're okay?
-Yeah.

01:02:24.699 --> 01:02:26.200
But how are you suddenly fine?

01:02:31.914 --> 01:02:33.291
Sheesh, that scared me.

01:02:35.209 --> 01:02:36.085
Damn.

01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:37.545
I'm beat.

01:02:48.556 --> 01:02:50.683
-Hello, Professor.
-Yeah.

01:03:09.577 --> 01:03:10.578
Hello.

01:03:10.661 --> 01:03:12.330
Hello, Professor.

01:03:21.339 --> 01:03:23.466
Professor! Hello.

01:05:01.480 --> 01:05:03.357
Mun-oh. Heo Mun-oh.

01:05:03.858 --> 01:05:05.234
You've lost it.

01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:07.028
Totally lost the plot.

01:05:12.742 --> 01:05:16.120
Mun-oh, what are you even doing?

01:05:17.538 --> 01:05:20.499
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

01:07:46.645 --> 01:07:51.650
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
